The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/agents/agents-01-actor-trait-registry-dispatch.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | Count | Key Concern |
|----------|-------|-------------|
| Critical | 0 | — |
| High | 1 | `ActorInterest` filtering declared but never enforced — all actors called every step, defeating documented ~60x optimization |
| Medium | 2 | Execution order is insertion-order convention only (no compile-time/declarative guarantee); `SolverFeedbackActor` is structurally special-cased outside the actors Vec |
| Low | 2 | Trait docs don't explain that `equipment_telemetry`/`equipment_core` in `EnvironmentState` are one-step-lagged snapshots; no debug assertion that actor Vec ordering is correct |

The main architectural strength is the cross-pass priority ledger in `ControlDispatcher` (Safety > Grid > UserOverride > Schedule persists across both dispatch passes within a timestep), which is well-tested in `dispatch_ordering_regressions.rs`. The main risk is that actor execution ordering relies entirely on insertion-order convention — the `ActorRegistry` provides no ordering guarantees at all, and `SolverFeedbackActor` runs first only because it's stored as a named field with explicit call sites.
